.TH ORO-IPC 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:ipc \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:ipc'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This is a low\-level API that you don't need unless you are implementing a library on top of Oro Runtime. An Oro app has one or more processes.
.PP
When you need to send a message to another window or to the backend, you should use the `application` module to get a reference to the window and use the `send` method to send a message.
.PP
\- The `Render` process, is the UI where the HTML, CSS, and JS are run. \- The `Bridge` process, is the thin layer of code that manages everything. \- The `Main` process, is for apps that need to run heavier compute jobs. And unlike electron it's optional.
.PP
The Bridge process manages the Render and Main process, it may also broker data between them.
.PP
The Binding process uses standard input and output as a way to communicate. Data written to the write\-end of the pipe is buffered by the OS until it is read from the read\-end of the pipe.
.PP
The IPC protocol uses a simple URI\-like scheme. Data is passed as ArrayBuffers.
.PP
ipc://command?key1=value1&key2=value2...
.PP
Example usage: import { send } from 'oro:ipc'
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBmaybeMakeError(error, caller)\fR
Converts a structured IPC error payload into an `Error` instance.
.br
Native responses sometimes serialize errors as plain objects. This helper rehydrates them into the closest matching runtime error type while preserving extra fields like `code`, `url`, and backend metadata.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIerror\fR (Error \\| { type?: string, code?: string \\| number, message?: string, [key: string]: any } \\| null \\| undefined; required)
.br
\fIcaller\fR (Function; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIError \\| null\fR
.TP
\fBconstructor(params, nonce)\fR
Documented method exposed by this module.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIparams\fR (object \\| any; required) Either a params object or a bare value which becomes `value`.
.br
\fInonce\fR (string \\| number \\| null; optional; default null) Optional nonce to include.
.TP
\fBemit(name, value, target, options)\fR
