\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIany\fR
.TP
\fBIPCMessagePort (extends MessagePort)\fR
A message port abstraction implemented using BroadcastChannel under the hood. This mirrors the MessagePort surface where practical and enables structured clone + transfer of ArrayBuffers and nested IPCMessagePorts. Emitted when a message is received by this port. Emitted when an error occurs while processing a message.
.TP
\fBfrom(options)\fR
Create or retrieve an IPCMessagePort from options.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR ({ id?: string, rx?: string, tx?: string, transferred?: boolean }; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIIPCMessagePort\fR
.TP
\fBtransfer(port)\fR
Mark a port as transferred (used when passing through postMessage).
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIport\fR (IPCMessagePort; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIIPCMessagePort\fR
.TP
\fBcreate(options)\fR
Create a new IPCMessagePort instance from options.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR ({ id?: string, rx?: string, tx?: string, transferred?: boolean }; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIIPCMessagePort\fR
.TP
\fBstart()\fR
Start the port; subsequent messages are delivered to listeners.
.TP
\fBclose()\fR
Close the port and release references.
.TP
